bitscan-agent (0.5.7-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release 0.5.7 of the Bitscan agent, with manager 0.5.7 (its code is
    unchanged from 0.5.0).
  * cmax-helper runs the ClusterMAX audit with HOME=/root, as sudo would,
    so cloud, Docker and enroot credentials are found. ClusterMAX writes
    its report files to /run/cmax-work (CLUSTERMAX_RUNS_ROOT), which the
    helper empties after each run.
  * PYTHONPATH=/usr/lib/clustermax/site, so check scripts that run with the
    system python3 find the bundled PyYAML (k8s_scheduling.status).
  * /usr/local/cuda/bin is on PATH, so the ncu and nvcc checks find the
    CUDA tools.
  * cmax-helper.service: MemoryMax=4G and CPUQuota=200% (were 1G and 50%),
    for large Slurm and Kubernetes clusters.
  * Supported with manager 0.5.7 and manager 0.5.6. Manager 0.5.7 supports
    agents 0.5.7-1 and 0.5.6-1.

 -- Bitdeer-Security <kaiquan.koh@bitdeer.com>  Sat, 21 Nov 2026 06:00:00 +0000

bitscan-agent (0.5.6-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release 0.5.6 of the Bitscan agent, with manager 0.5.6 (its code is
    unchanged from 0.5.0).
  * cmax-helper runs the ClusterMAX audit with KUBECONFIG set to the first
    of /root/.kube/config, /etc/rancher/k3s/k3s.yaml,
    /etc/rancher/rke2/rke2.yaml and /etc/kubernetes/admin.conf that exists,
    with /var/lib/rancher/rke2/bin, /opt/slurm/bin and /snap/bin on PATH,
    and with SLURM_CONF when slurm.conf is only in /etc/slurm-llnl or
    /opt/slurm/etc. The audit then finds Slurm or Kubernetes as a root
    shell on the host would.
  * cmax-helper answers "get <run> wait" with done or running. The
    ClusterMAX policy has 10 new wait plugins, so a long audit on a large
    cluster has about one hour before the checks time out.
  * Supported with manager 0.5.6 and manager 0.5.5. Manager 0.5.6 supports
    agents 0.5.6-1 and 0.5.5-1.

