bitscan-agent (0.5.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release 0.5.1 of the Bitscan agent, with manager 0.5.1 (its code is
    unchanged from 0.5.0).
  * postinst now enables and starts bitscan-capread.socket on every host,
    so the checks that read the firewall, audit and AppArmor state work
    after install. bitscan-capread.service is still started only by its
    socket. A root user can turn it off with
    "systemctl disable --now bitscan-capread.socket"; later upgrades keep
    it off. The upgrade from 0.5.0-1 or older turns it on for every host.
  * postinst starts cmax-helper.socket and bitscan-capread.socket before
    bitscan-agent.service, so the first heartbeat after an install or
    upgrade reports "cmax" and "capread" in runner_helpers.
  * The package has no preinst any more: its only snippet stopped the old
    disabled capread units before an upgrade.
  * The binaries and units are unchanged from 0.5.0-1.
  * Supported with manager 0.5.1 and manager 0.5.0. Manager 0.5.1 supports
    agents 0.5.1-1 and 0.5.0-1.
  * Upgrades 0.5.0-1 and older in place and keeps their configuration,
    agent token and agent id.

