bitscan-agent (0.5.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release 0.5.0 of the Bitscan agent, with manager 0.5.0.
  * Compliance jobs of different policies run at the same time, at most
    max_parallel_jobs at once (agent.yaml, default 2, 1 to 4; manager 0.5.0
    sends its setting in the heartbeat). Jobs wait in pull order, and two
    jobs that share a check (the same policy, or a job and its retry) never
    run at the same time.
  * The runner serves up to 4 jobs at once. Each job gets the cgroup
    plugins/j-<n>, inside the shared plugins task limit, and its own temp
    directory /tmp/bitscan-j-<random>. The end of a job cleans only that
    job; the full cleanup of the runner's cgroups and of its private /tmp
    and /var/tmp runs when no job runs.
  * The package now includes the ClusterMAX collector: cmax-helper, the
    cmax-trigger client and ClusterMAX 0.3.0 (Apache-2.0) under
    /usr/lib/clustermax, and depends on python3 (>= 3.10). postinst turns on
    cmax-helper.socket on every host; a scan of the ClusterMAX policy then
    runs "cmax audit -vvv -y" as root on the targeted host, once per scan,
    with the report held only in memory. A root user can turn it off with
    "systemctl disable --now cmax-helper.socket"; upgrades keep it off.
  * The heartbeat reports "cmax" in runner_helpers while the collector
    socket /run/clustermax/collect.sock exists. The agent never connects
    to it.
  * New installs write max_parallel_jobs: 2 to agent.yaml. An upgraded host
    keeps its agent.yaml; without the key the agent uses 2.
  * The agent and runner units are unchanged; cmax-helper.socket and
    cmax-helper.service are new.
  * Supported with manager 0.5.0 and manager 0.4.1. Manager 0.5.0 supports
    agents 0.5.0-1 and 0.4.1-1.
  * Upgrades 0.4.1-1 and 0.4.0-1 in place and keeps their configuration,
    agent token and agent id.

 -- Bitdeer-Security <kaiquan.koh@bitdeer.com>  Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000

bitscan-agent (0.4.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release 0.4.1 of the Bitscan agent, with manager 0.4.1.
  * Fix: on hosts with many CPUs (seen on 256) the runner could die in the
    middle of a scan ("failed to create new OS thread") and report every
    remaining check runner_unavailable. A Go program a check ran, such as
    the bitscan-capread client, sized itself to every CPU on the host and
    started about 64 threads in the runner's 64-task limit.
  * Each plugin cgroup now carries the runner unit's CPU limit (cpu.max),
    so a Go program a check runs starts with GOMAXPROCS=2 whatever the CPU
    count.
  * All plugin cgroups now sit under plugins/, which shares the unit's task
    limit less 16 (48 with TasksMax=64), so checks together can never take
    the tasks the runner needs. A check that ran while that limit refused a
    process is reported truncated (ERROR), never PASS or FAIL.
  * The bitscan-capread client keeps to one P.
  * The units are unchanged. The manager code is unchanged from 0.4.0 apart
    from its version.
  * Supported with manager 0.4.1 and manager 0.4.0. Manager 0.4.1 supports
    agents 0.4.1-1 and 0.4.0-1.
  * Upgrades 0.4.0-1 and 0.3.0-1 in place and keeps their configuration,
    agent token and agent id.

 -- Bitdeer-Security <kaiquan.koh@bitdeer.com>  Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000

bitscan-agent (0.4.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release 0.4.0 of the Bitscan agent, with manager 0.4.0.
  * The optional bitscan-capread helper answers a third fixed request,
    apparmor_profiles: it reads /sys/kernel/security/apparmor/profiles
    itself (the kernel opens that file only for uid or gid 0) and returns
    one "name (mode)" line per loaded AppArmor profile. Its unit adds
    SupplementaryGroups=root for this; it still runs as a throwaway
    non-root user with only CAP_NET_ADMIN and CAP_AUDIT_CONTROL, stays off
    until an administrator enables it on the host, and never takes a
    command line or a path. Accepted risk: on a host where the helper is
    enabled, a compromise of the helper could read files that group root
    can read.
  * The manager code is unchanged from 0.3.0 apart from its version.
  * Supported with manager 0.4.0 and manager 0.3.0. Manager 0.4.0 supports
    agents 0.4.0-1 and 0.3.0-1.
  * Upgrades 0.3.0-1 and 0.2.0-1 in place and keeps their configuration,
    agent token and agent id.

 -- Bitdeer-Security <kaiquan.koh@bitdeer.com>  Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000

bitscan-agent (0.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release 0.3.0 of the Bitscan agent, with manager 0.3.0. The agent
    code is unchanged from 0.2.0-1; this package carries the new version
    so that the agent and the manager are released together.
  * Manager 0.3.0 keeps a web UI user signed in across a page reload: the
    session token lives in an HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite=Strict cookie
    that page scripts cannot read, with a required X-Bitscan-Request
    header and an Origin check against cross-site requests. A new
    "My sessions" page lists the user's own web sessions and ends any of
    them. Agents and their tokens are not affected.
  * Supported with manager 0.3.0 and manager 0.2.0. Manager 0.3.0
    supports agents 0.3.0-1 and 0.2.0-1; hosts still on 0.1.0-1 must be
    upgraded to 0.2.0-1 or later before the manager is upgraded.
  * Upgrades 0.2.0-1 in place and keeps its configuration, agent token
    and agent id.

